# Photograph the level table printed by five prestige classes.
#
# The tables are player-facing prose that sits in the same file as the class's
# own Flags and Def: field, so the three can disagree -- and in these five they
# did. See bd inc-tek.8.3, findings PA-03-F16 (three classes printed their save
# columns transposed) and PA-03-F17 (two printed a defence track their class
# does not grant). tools/check_prestige_tables.sh reads these dumps.
#
# The prestige menu is the right screen to read them from because it shows the
# class's Desc: exactly as a player choosing a class sees it. Nothing here
# takes a prestige class; the menu only highlights.
#
# HOW IT GETS THERE. Free Advancement is a wizard-mode switch, so the script
# enters wizard mode (lowercase w -- 'W' is a different keystroke, see
# TokenToKey in src/Wposix.cpp), turns the switch on, and then uses the
# character sheet's [G] to reach the three core levels that
# src/Managers.cpp:2252 demands before it will open the prestige list.
#
# SEED-INDEPENDENT for what it asserts. The menu letters and the DOWN counts
# below depend on the number of prestige classes in lib/, not on the seed, and
# the descriptions are static text. The chargen it includes is seed-locked,
# which is why a seed is still passed.

@include chargen-rogue.keys

ESC             # dismiss the arrival-room description
w               # wizard mode
y               # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w               # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN       # Cheat Death -> Auto-Identify Items -> Free Advancement
SPACE           # NO -> YES
ESC             # leave the options manager

d               # character sheet
G G G           # three core levels; the prestige list refuses fewer

# The list opens on [a] Alienist. DOWN walks it in letter order:
#   a Alienist   b Assassin   c Blackguard   d Bladesinger  e Celestial Initiate
#   f Crimson Adept  g Duelist  h Earthsinger  i Elementalist  j Horizon Walker
#   k Inquisitor  l Loremaster  m Master Archer  n Sentinel  o Shadowdancer
#   p Tattoo Mystic  q Twilight Huntsman  r Undead Slayer  s Underdark Warrior
#
# Each class scrolls to its own table with @until, which is proof against the
# descriptions changing length. The extra PGDNs bring the rows themselves into
# view; the @until stops as soon as the header appears on the last line.
P

@until "Special Abilities" PGDN
PGDN*8
@dump:alienist

DOWN DOWN                       # [c] Blackguard
@until "Special Abilities" PGDN
PGDN*8
@dump:blackguard

DOWN*9                          # [l] Loremaster
@until "Special Abilities" PGDN
PGDN*8
@dump:loremaster

DOWN DOWN                       # [n] Sentinel
@until "Special Abilities" PGDN
PGDN*4                          # this table is four rows and then "..."
@dump:sentinel

DOWN*3                          # [q] Twilight Huntsman
@until "Special Abilities" PGDN
PGDN*8
@dump:twilight

ESC
@quit
